---
// The color editor guide, shown under "Add custom colors" in the Builder
// Guide (src/pages/website-builder/index.astro).
import { paletteImportExample, paletteShades } from "../../../data/website-builder/palette.js";
---

<p>
  Choose the <strong>websitebuilder project folder</strong> to add or remove
  color families. You can also choose its <code>src</code> folder to add or
  import families. Both options save to{" "}
  <code>src/styles/themes/colors.css</code>.
</p>
<p>
  This requires a browser that supports the File System Access API, such as
  Chrome or Edge, and a secure connection or localhost. Files are read locally
  and are not uploaded.
</p>
<p>
  The editor remembers your folder for this tab and reconnects after a
  development-page reload. If your browser asks for permission again, select{" "}
  <strong>Reconnect project</strong>; you do not need to find the folder again.
</p>

<section aria-labelledby="import-format-title" class="min-w-0">
  <h3 id="import-format-title" class="font-semibold">
    Import color families from text files
  </h3>
  <p id="import-format-help">
    Choose one or more plain-text UTF-8 files ending in .txt or .css, up to 1 MB
    combined. Use one declaration per line in the format
    <code>--color-FAMILY-SHADE: oklch(L% C H);</code>. L is lightness (0-100%),
    C is chroma (0 or greater), and H is hue (0-360 degrees). Include the
    semicolon after every color.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each family needs all 11 shades: {paletteShades.join(", ")}. Use a unique
    lowercase family name starting with a letter, with letters, numbers, and
    single hyphens between words (up to 60 characters). Do not use built-in
    names such as blue or red, existing family names, or the reserved names
    custom, theme, none, and solid. Do not repeat a shade within the same
    family.
  </p>
  <p>
    For multiple families, put each complete set in the same file or select
    several files together using Ctrl-click (Command-click on Mac) or
    Shift-click. Every family needs a different name. CSS wrappers such as :root
    are optional; JSON, commas, and code fences are not needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose your project folder or its <code>src</code> folder, then use{" "}
    <strong>Import color families</strong>
    below. Review families using the selector, then click{" "}
    <strong>Save all imported families to colors.css</strong> to save every
    family from all selected files at once. Your name and shade edits are
    included. Nothing is saved if any family is invalid or already exists. Use{" "}
    <strong>Add family</strong> to save only the selected family instead.
  </p>
  <details class="min-w-0">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer">
      Example .txt file with two complete families
    </summary>
    <pre class="mt-4 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded border border-canvas-page-border p-4 text-sm"><code>{paletteImportExample}</code></pre>
  </details>
  <a
    class="w-fit wrap-anywhere underline"
    href={`data:text/plain;charset=utf-8,${encodeURIComponent(paletteImportExample + "\n")}`}
    download="color-families.txt"
  >
    Download example color-families.txt
  </a>
</section>
